 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Fran wants to take a new job but will have to move to an area with a higher cost of living. With her current income, she can use the 50-30-20 budget philosophy. The new job will have a net pay of $43,700 annually. She will still have to pay her car payment of $295.00, her student loans that cost $264.00 per month, and her outstanding credit card debt, on which she pays $200 per month.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519216,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Apply the 50-30-20 budget philosophy to Fran’s new income.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The 50-30-20 principle suggests spending 50 percent of your budget on necessary expenses (basic living requirements and debt services such as mortgage/rent, utilities, car, insurance, health care, groceries, gasoline, child care, and minimum debt payments), 30 percent of your budget for wants (restaurants, vacations, hobby costs), and 20 percent should be set aside (retirement funds, stocks, an emergency fund should have at least 3 months of income, other investments).</p>\n<p>Monthly income = $43,700 / 12</p>\n<p>The monthly income: $3,641.66.</p>\n<p>Spend 50 percent on needs. Fifty percent is $1,820.83.</p>\n<p>Spend 30 percent on wants. Thirty percent is $1,092.50.</p>\n<p>Set aside 20 percent in savings, investments, and debt service. Twenty percent is $728.33.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Her monthly income is $3,641.66.<br>\nNeeds (50%): $1,820.83, Wants (30%): $1,092.50, Savings (20%): $728.33"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 519217,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "If she follows the budget, how much does she have, after paying her credit card debt, car payment and student loan, to spend on necessities.",
